From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Star7-ROM <star7@rom.local>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 10:15:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add EAD call-site shim to SemMdnieManager

The EnvironmentAdaptiveDisplay APK (com.samsung.android.sead) calls
SemMdnieManager;->setEadMode(I[I)V / setEadModeSub(I[I)V, the API 35
two-argument shape. The One UI 8.5 (API 36) donor framework bumped both
methods to three arguments (setEadMode(II[I)V), so the APK's call site no
longer resolves and sead dies with NoSuchMethodError:

  java.lang.NoSuchMethodError: No virtual method setEadMode(I[I)V in class
  Lcom/samsung/android/hardware/display/SemMdnieManager;

No newer Samsung build restores the two-argument form, so re-declare it
here as a thin overload that forwards to the three-argument method with a
default index of 0. This keeps the stock binder ABI (ISemMdnieManager and
SemMdnieManagerService stay untouched, exactly as stock) and only re-adds
the client surface the APK links against.
---

1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/smali_classes6/com/samsung/android/hardware/display/SemMdnieManager.smali b/smali_classes6/com/samsung/android/hardware/display/SemMdnieManager.smali
--- a/smali_classes6/com/samsung/android/hardware/display/SemMdnieManager.smali
+++ b/smali_classes6/com/samsung/android/hardware/display/SemMdnieManager.smali
@@ -679,6 +679,26 @@
     return v0
 .end method
 
+.method public blacklist setEadMode(I[I)V
+    .locals 1
+
+    const/4 v0, 0x0
+
+    invoke-virtual {p0, p1, v0, p2}, Lcom/samsung/android/hardware/display/SemMdnieManager;->setEadMode(II[I)V
+
+    return-void
+.end method
+
+.method public blacklist setEadModeSub(I[I)V
+    .locals 1
+
+    const/4 v0, 0x0
+
+    invoke-virtual {p0, p1, v0, p2}, Lcom/samsung/android/hardware/display/SemMdnieManager;->setEadModeSub(II[I)V
+
+    return-void
+.end method
+
 .method public blacklist setEadMode(II[I)V
     .locals 1
 
